  "response": "```python\ndef reverse_list_elements(elements, punctuation):\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the order of elements while maintaining the associated punctuation.\n\n    Args:\n        elements (list): List of elements (strings)\n        punctuation (list): List of punctuation marks corresponding to each element\n\n    Returns:\n        tuple: (new_elements, new_punctuation) - both lists reversed\n    \"\"\"\n    # Reverse both lists while maintaining their index pairing\n    new_elements = elements[::-1]\n    new_punctuation = punctuation[::-1]\n    \n    return (new_elements, new_punctuation)\n```\n\n### Example Usage:\n```python\n# Basic example\nelements = [\"Hello\", \"world\"]\npunctuation = [\"\", \"!\"]\nresult = reverse_list_elements(elements, punctuation)\nprint(result)  # (['world', 'Hello'], ['!', ''])\n\n# With multiple punctuation marks\nelements2 = [\"Hi\", \"Bye!\", \"How?\"]\npunctuation2 = [\".\", \",\", \"?\"]\nresult2 = reverse_list_elements(elements2, punctuation2)\nprint(result2)  # (['How?', 'Bye!', 'Hi'], ['?', ',', '.'])\n\n# With empty list\nelements3 = []\npunctuation3 = []\nresult3 = reverse_list_elements(elements3, punctuation3)\nprint(result3)  # ([], [])\n\n# Mixed content\nelements4 = [\"Apple\", \"Banana!\", \"Cherry??\"]\npunctuation4 = [\" \", \".?\", \".\"]\nresult4 = reverse_list_elements(elements4, punctuation4)\nprint(result4)  # (['Cherry??', 'Banana!', 'Apple'], ['.', '?', ' '])\n```",
